  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Visitor journey",
      "items": [
        "The server reads saved catalogs and renders the homepage and repository routes. Client components handle category filters, previews, Lab selection, comparisons and keyboard navigation.",
        "Skills and MCP pages request /api/skills and /api/mcp, then filter locally. Those entries link to upstream documentation; MarketAtlas does not run the indexed tools."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "violet",
      "title": "Search stays local",
      "items": [
        "The root layout builds one index from the financial catalog and passes it to the command palette. Typing performs case-insensitive, multi-word matching in memory.",
        "/api/search is a separate read-only interface using the same search functions; the palette does not call it. Project results use internal detail routes; Skills and MCP results open upstream sources."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Saved data, explicit refresh",
      "items": [
        "Catalog reads prefer data/cache.json and fall back to bundled data/catalog.json on read or parse errors. Weekly reads prefer data/weekly-cache.json, validate ten entries, and fall back to data/github-weekly.json on error.",
        "Refresh commands are operator-run. discover.ts preserves previous entries on individual failures; refresh-weekly.ts validates ten repositories before atomically replacing files. --snapshot also updates the bundled fallback.",
        "Financial seven-day growth uses recorded observations. GitHub Lab uses reported weekly stars from GitHub Trending selection, not an exhaustive ranking of every repository."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "External services & boundaries",
      "items": [
        "TradingView loads directly in the browser. Quotes remain in its iframe; equities are labeled delayed. The host handles loading failures and retry, not market-data storage.",
        "Repository detail routes attempt a GitHub README request; browsing catalogs and typing search do not trigger GitHub discovery. GITHUB_TOKEN is optional and remains server-side.",
        "Favorites and theme preferences stay on the visitor device. The current application has no connected database or account backend; the optional SQL schema is not part of this runtime."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "slate",
      "title": "Source and release scope",
      "items": [
        "Every node includes inspected source ranges pinned to a published GitHub commit. Open a node to review its source files. This standalone diagram describes that committed application snapshot.",
        "This is a source-backed application overview, not a live deployment topology. GitHub Actions validates tests, build and types; it does not schedule catalog refresh. Vercel infrastructure details are intentionally outside this source map."
      ]
    }
  ]
